    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d395">

                <pb facs="0323" n="311" xml:id="pg311"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111A.R./1061: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Beaulac</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-05-14T15:00:00-05:00">May 14, 1940—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:37 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>46. The Secretary of State<anchor n="75" xml:id="d395-f1"/> showed me this
                    morning two draft decrees he is submitting to the President<anchor n="76"
                        xml:id="d395-f2"/> providing for the internment of submarines which may have
                    engaged in belligerent activities within the American neutrality zone and
                    providing that Cuba shall adopt an attitude of “benevolent neutrality” toward
                    countries that may have been invaded without provocation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Beaulac</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
